sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor S as Sender
  participant API as API (Hono on Bun)
  participant P as policy.ts
  participant ST as storage.ts
  participant S3 as S3 Bucket
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant WS as Socket.IO Gateway
  actor R as Recipient

  S->>S: client-side check: size, count, MIME allowlist
  S->>API: POST /api/chats/:chatId/messages (multipart)
  API->>API: bodyLimit ~51 MB
  API->>DB: requireChatMember - membership + chat row
  DB-->>API: member, chat
  alt not a member
    API-->>S: 404 (never 403 - existence is not confirmed)
  end

  API->>P: sendBlock(chat, member)
  P-->>API: null | MUTED | READ_ONLY | ARCHIVED
  alt blocked
    API-->>S: 403 with the same sentence the UI shows
  end

  API->>ST: storeUploads(files)
  ST->>ST: per file - size, MIME allowlist, magic bytes
  ST->>ST: key = YYYY-MM / UUIDv7 / safe display name
  ST->>S3: PUT object (Bun.S3Client)
  S3-->>ST: stored
  ST-->>API: StoredFile[] (bucket + key recorded per row)

  rect rgb(240, 246, 252)
    Note over API,DB: single transaction
    API->>DB: insert message + attachments
    API->>DB: bump chats.last_message_at
    API->>DB: insert DELIVERED receipts for every other member
  end

  alt transaction fails
    API->>S3: delete the orphaned objects
    API-->>S: error
  end

  API->>WS: emitToChat(chatId, "message:new", dto)
  Note right of WS: emitted only after commit,<br/>so a rollback cannot produce a phantom message
  WS--)R: message:new
  WS--)S: message:new (own echo, applied by id)
  API-->>S: 201 MessageDto

  R->>R: IntersectionObserver marks it seen
  R->>API: POST /messages/read {upToMessageId} (batched)
  API->>DB: advance receipts DELIVERED -> READ
  API->>WS: receipt:read
  WS--)S: tick marks fill in
